From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:02:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] downloads: never drop an episode silently; reuse or
 replace folders left on disk
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Same change as mihon-harmony 0011. Tapping "download" on an episode did
nothing when a folder for it already existed on disk although the episode
list showed it as not downloaded: Downloader.queueEpisodes filtered such
episodes out with a storage lookup, so the button flashed and the queue
stayed empty. On 卓易通 this happens after an interrupted finalisation
(process frozen or killed while the video was being moved into the final
folder) because the download cache only learns about folders on its hourly
renewal.

- queueEpisodes decides "already downloaded" from the download cache (the
  same information the episode list shows) and reports what happened:
  queued / already downloaded / already in the queue / source not
  installed. DownloadManager adds the count of fillermarked episodes it
  dropped because of the "deny downloading of fillermarked episodes"
  setting, which used to be silent as well.
- downloadEpisode checks the disk before creating the temporary directory:
  a folder with one non-empty video is registered in the cache as
  downloaded without re-downloading; a video still waiting in the _tmp
  directory means the move was interrupted, so the final copy is only
  trusted when it has the same size. Anything else is removed and the
  download starts again (reusing whatever is left in _tmp).
- The anime screen shows a snackbar when episodes were not queued, with
  the reason.

Episodes already in the queue in ERROR state are reported as `retried`,
not as skipped: tapping a failed episode re-queues it through this path
and the caller restarts the downloader (mihon-harmony 0011 + 0013).

Differs from Mihon in the completeness rule: an episode is one video file
(plus .nomedia), there is no page count to compare against.
